# conductor:ui - Conductor's web interface, sandbox plane only.
#
# Two differences from ./Dockerfile, which this pull request does not touch, so
# the development, staging and production builds provably cannot change.
#
# First, the base is pinned. ./Dockerfile says plainly "FROM nginx", with no
# version at all, so what gets built depends entirely on what the registry's
# moving tag points at that day — the same source has produced different images
# on different days, and nobody can tell from the repository which one is
# running.
#
# Second, it is the Alpine variant rather than the Debian one. Every one of the
# eighteen critical findings the scanner reports against the sandbox's current
# web-interface image is an operating-system package, five of them flagged as
# having a known exploit, and the two worst offenders are perl and openssl.
# The Alpine variant does not ship perl at all and carries a far smaller
# package set, so this is the change that actually clears them rather than
# waiting for the Debian base to be patched.
#
# The interface serves static files and proxies to the server; it holds no
# credential and runs no application code of ours, so the base swap carries
# little behavioural risk. The one thing to confirm on the first build is that
# nginx's user is still uid 101 — the plane's chart pins runAsUser to 101 and
# mounts its cache and pid directories as emptyDirs on that assumption
# (k8s/mesta-services/conductor-ui/sandbox/nginx-writable.yaml in the
# infrastructure repository). If Alpine ever moves that uid, pin
# nginx:1.29.8-trixie instead and accept the larger package set.
FROM nginx:1.29.8-alpine3.23
COPY default.conf /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf
COPY build/ /usr/share/nginx/html
